# The certificates an AerieOS release's Android app may be signed by: the
# SHA-256 fingerprint of each, one a line, as apksigner and a release's
# notes write it (colons or none, either case). A line after # is a comment.
#
# The app is the one file of a release no build attests: its build hands it
# over unsigned, and a controller signs it with the app's own key and
# attaches it afterwards (scripts/dashboard/releasesign.py). So what says a
# release's APK is AerieOS's is that signature, and the release's list of
# files is signed only over an APK apksigner verifies as signed by a
# certificate named here (tools/release-sign.py, its one reader). The
# fingerprint is public: every release's notes give it.
#
# A key rotated to a new one adds the new certificate's line under the old,
# in the commit that maps the app to the new key.
